  "definition": "Exempt modification",
  "effectiveDate": "2026-09-01",
  "expirationDate": "2036-09-01",
  "historyNote": "#14657, eff 9-1-26, EXPIRES: 9-1-36",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "En 1002.20",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1000.html",
  "prefLabel": "En 1002.20 Exempt modification",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 1002.20 “Exempt modification” means a modification to an application or facility that does not increase the export capacity of the facility, relocate the point of interconnection (POI), or otherwise qualify as a material modification. These include, but are not limited to:\n\n(a) A change of ownership of a facility;\n\n(b) A change or replacement of generating equipment, including inverters and transformers, that is a like-kind substitution in size, ratings, impedances, efficiencies, or capabilities of the equipment;\n\n(c) Replacement of existing inverters with inverters that conform to more recent standards after the state has adopted their use, as long as the export capacity does not increase;\n\n(d) Any change to equipment on the direct current (DC) side of the applicant’s equipment, including DC coupled storage;\n\n(e) Any change to relays or reclosers that do not alter trip settings;\n\n(f) Modification to the grounding configuration that remains in compliance with utility standards;\n\n(g) A change where the inverter dynamic simulation performance is equivalent to the existing inverter; and\n\n(h) A reduction in the size of the facility.\n\nSource. #14657, eff 9-1-26, EXPIRES: 9-1-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1000.html"
